    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <div class="effective">
        Effective: October 6, 2026
    </div>

    <div class="intro">
        <p>
            At PLACIDATE™, privacy is built into the authentication process.
            PLACIDATE™ is an authentication and account-recovery service developed
            by Anescribe, L.L.C. for electronic medical record systems and other
            authorized systems.
        </p>

        <p>
            This Privacy Policy describes how PLACIDATE™ handles information when
            a user scans the PDF417 barcode on a U.S. driver's license or other
            supported government-issued identification.
        </p>
    </div>


    <h2>1. Information Contained in Your ID Barcode</h2>

    <p>
        The PDF417 barcode on a government-issued ID may contain considerably more
        information than PLACIDATE™ needs to provide authentication.
    </p>

    <p>
        Depending on the issuing jurisdiction, that information may include a
        person's name, full date of birth, residential address, physical
        characteristics, driver's-license information, and other identifying data.
    </p>

    <div class="highlight">
        <p>
            PLACIDATE™ is designed to minimize the information retained from your
            identification barcode.
        </p>
    </div>


    <h2>2. Information PLACIDATE™ Retains</h2>

    <p>
        PLACIDATE™ is designed to retain only the information needed for its
        authentication function:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>Your name; and</li>
        <li>Your birthday, limited to the <strong>month and day of birth</strong>.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        PLACIDATE™ does <strong>not intentionally retain your year of birth.</strong>
    </p>


    <h2>3. Information We Do Not Intentionally Retain</h2>

    <p>
        PLACIDATE™ is designed not to retain information from your ID barcode
        that is unnecessary for authentication, including:
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li>Your residential or mailing address;</li>
        <li>Your year of birth;</li>
        <li>Your weight;</li>
        <li>Hair or eye color;</li>
        <li>Height or other physical descriptors;</li>
        <li>Driver's-license number;</li>
        <li>Driver's-license class, restrictions, or endorsements; or</li>
        <li>Driving history, traffic violations, or similar driving-record information.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        Some of these data elements may be read or processed transiently when the
        barcode is scanned and decoded. PLACIDATE™ is designed to discard
        information that is not required for its authentication function rather
        than store it as part of your PLACIDATE™ record.
    </p>


    <h2>4. How We Use Retained Information</h2>

    <p>
        Information retained by PLACIDATE™ is used only to provide, maintain,
        secure, troubleshoot, and improve authentication and account-recovery
        services.
    </p>

    <p>
        We do not sell information obtained through PLACIDATE™.
    </p>

    <p>
        We do not use driver's-license or identification information for
        advertising or third-party marketing.
    </p>


    <h2>5. EMRs and Other Integrating Systems</h2>

    <p>
        PLACIDATE™ may be integrated into an electronic medical record system,
        website, application, or other service operated by another organization.
    </p>

    <p>
        That organization may separately collect, store, or process information
        about you. Its handling of information is governed by its own privacy
        practices and is outside the control of PLACIDATE™ and Anescribe, L.L.C.
    </p>

    <p>
        Organizations integrating PLACIDATE™ are responsible for appropriately
        configuring and securing their own systems and for complying with applicable
        privacy, security, employment, professional, and other legal requirements.
    </p>


    <h2>6. Data Security and Data Minimization</h2>

    <p>
        PLACIDATE™ uses technical and administrative safeguards designed to protect
        information processed through the service.
    </p>

    <div class="highlight">
        <p>
            <strong>An important part of our security approach is data minimization:</strong>
            information that PLACIDATE™ does not need is designed not to be retained.
        </p>
    </div>

    <p>
        No software, device, network, or data-processing system can guarantee
        absolute security. Although PLACIDATE™ is designed to discard unnecessary
        information contained in an identification barcode, we cannot guarantee
        that such information could never be unintentionally exposed as the result
        of a software defect, compromised device, unauthorized access, security
        incident, third-party system, or other circumstance.
    </p>

    <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, Anescribe, L.L.C. is
        not responsible for unauthorized disclosure caused by an integrating
        organization's systems, a user's device or conduct, third-party systems
        outside our control, or other circumstances outside our reasonable control.
    </p>

    <p>
        Nothing in this Privacy Policy limits any obligation or liability that
        cannot lawfully be limited or excluded.
    </p>


    <h2>7. Data Retention</h2>

    <p>
        PLACIDATE™ retains information only for as long as reasonably necessary to
        provide authentication and account-recovery services, maintain security and
        audit records, support users, comply with applicable legal requirements,
        resolve disputes, and protect the service against misuse.
    </p>

    <p>
        Information that PLACIDATE™ is not designed to retain is not intentionally
        maintained as part of the user's PLACIDATE™ authentication record.
    </p>


    <h2>8. No Sale of Personal Information</h2>

    <p>
        PLACIDATE™ does not sell personal information obtained through identification
        scans.
    </p>

    <p>
        Information obtained through PLACIDATE™ is not shared with third parties
        for third-party advertising or marketing.
    </p>


    <h2>9. United States Only</h2>

    <p>
        PLACIDATE™ is intended for use in the United States with supported U.S.
        government-issued identification.
    </p>


    <h2>10. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>

    <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy as PLACIDATE™ develops. Updates will be
        posted on this page with a revised effective date.
    </p>


